# Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star (repertoire plan: twinkle-twinkle-little-star). The French air
# "Ah! vous dirai-je, maman" with Jane Taylor's words, in G in first position: 12 bars in A B A
# form (the middle line is played twice, then the first line returns).
# Notes: G = open string 3, A = string 3 fret 2 (finger 2), B = open string 2, C = string 2
# fret 1 (finger 1), D = string 2 fret 3 (finger 3), E = open string 1. The jump in bar 1 from
# G up to D crosses from string 3 to string 2. The teacher strums G, C and D7.
title: Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star
id: twinkle-twinkle-little-star
composer: Traditional French (melody); words by Jane Taylor
source: Tune printed in 1761 (Ah! vous dirai-je, maman); words 1806; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (anonymous tune of 1761; words by Jane Taylor, died 1824); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: melody, lyrics, nursery rhyme, beginner
tempo: 92
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Melody
role: lead
[A]
| "G" q 3:0 3:0 2:3{3} 2:3 | "C" q 1:0 1:0 "G" h 2:3 | "C" q 2:1{1} 2:1 "G" 2:0 2:0 | "D7" q 3:2{2} 3:2 "G" h 3:0 |
lyrics: Twin- kle, twin- kle, lit- tle star, how I won- der what you are.
[B]
| "G" q 2:3 2:3 "C" 2:1 2:1 | "G" q 2:0 2:0 "D7" h 3:2 | "G" q 2:3 2:3 "C" 2:1 2:1 | "G" q 2:0 2:0 "D7" h 3:2 |
lyrics: Up a- bove the world so high, like a dia- mond in the sky.
[A again]
| "G" q 3:0 3:0 2:3 2:3 | "C" q 1:0 1:0 "G" h 2:3 | "C" q 2:1 2:1 "G" 2:0 2:0 | "D7" q 3:2 3:2 "G" h 3:0 ||
lyrics: Twin- kle, twin- kle, lit- tle star, how I won- der what you are.

